    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d47">

                <pb facs="0114" n="46" sameAs="frus:frus1914-20v01/pg46"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72115/2612</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        President Wilson
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-12-07">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 7, 1916</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. President</hi>: I enclose herewith a
                    confidential telegram received from Mr. Grew<anchor n="20" xml:id="d47-f1"/> in
                    answer to our telegram of November 29th<anchor n="21" xml:id="d47-f2"/>—which is
                    the one we took such care to prevent from becoming public.</p>
                <pb facs="0115" n="47" xml:id="pg47"/>
                <p>I cannot say that I find Mr. Grew’s telegram very encouraging but I suppose no
                    judgment should be formed until the Chancellor has had an opportunity to consult
                    with Mr. Zimmermann and make a formal answer.</p>
                <p>Faithfully yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
